1897–98 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s tenth season of competitive football. They competed in [[Scottish Division One]], which they won for the fourth time.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1890/celtic1898.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1897-98|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> It was the fifth major domestic honour in the club's history. [[Dan Doyle (footballer)|Dan Doyle]], who had been playing for the club since 1891, became its second ever captain this season as [[James Kelly (footballer, born 1865)|James Kelly]] had retired.

